{%- case gem_handle -%}

  {%- when 'navratana' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--navratana">
    <h2>Why Navratna Exists</h2>
    <b>Because Balance Is Different From Strength</b>
    <p>Most astrological gemstones are traditionally worn to strengthen a particular planetary influence.</p>
    <p>Navratna exists for a different reason.</p>
    <p>Rather than focusing on one force, it brings together all nine planetary gemstones within a single arrangement. The traditional belief is that harmony arises when each planetary influence is acknowledged and none is allowed to dominate the others.</p>
    <p>Its purpose is not to make one voice louder.</p>
    <p>It is to help the whole system remain balanced.</p>
  </div>

  {%- when 'upratnas' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--upratnas">
    <h2>Why Upratnas Exist</h2>
    <b>Because Tradition Allows More Than One Path</b>
    <p>Astrological traditions have always recognised that different people require different remedies.</p>
    <p>For some, a primary planetary gemstone may be recommended. For others, a supporting gemstone may be considered more suitable due to personal circumstances, comfort level, practicality, or astrological guidance.</p>
    <p>Upratna exist because traditional gemstone practice has never been based solely on rarity or price. It has always acknowledged that effectiveness, comfort, and suitability can take many forms.</p>
    <p>These gemstones allow individuals to participate in a centuries-old tradition while respecting their own preferences and circumstances.</p>
    <p>The purpose of an Upratna is not to be stronger.</p>
    <p>It is to be appropriate.</p>
  </div>

  {%- else -%}
  <div class="gem-tab">
    <p>[Placeholder] Content coming soon.</p>
  </div>

{%- endcase -%}
